    "summary_insights": [
      "Revenue demonstrated strong recovery in FY25, growing 31.1% following a 9% dip in FY24, indicating robust market demand.",
      "Gross margin improved significantly from 27.4% in FY23 to 37.8% in FY25, driven by the normalisation of raw material prices and internal manufacturing efficiencies.",
      "Net profit increased substantially from £229,952 to £1.9m over the period, representing a significant expansion in net margin from 1.5% to 10.4%.",
      "Operating profit (EBITDA) more than tripled between FY23 and FY25, reflecting successful operational scaling and cost control.",
      "Financial resilience has strengthened remarkably, with the interest coverage ratio improving from 6.9x to 45.5x as debt levels were reduced.",
      "The business successfully transitioned through a period of heavy investment in FY23, resulting in a leaner and more profitable cost structure in subsequent years.",
      "A qualified audit opinion regarding inventory verification in FY25 (£2.6m) represents a potential red flag for internal controls and valuation accuracy.",
      "Adjusted EBITDA, the basis for sale, shows a consistent upward trajectory, reaching nearly £3m by FY25."
    ]
