    "summary_insights": [
      "The company demonstrates a significantly strengthening asset base, with net assets growing by 36.4% in FY25, driven by strong retained profitability.",
      "Liquidity is robust and improving; the current ratio increased to 2.78 in FY25, while the quick ratio rose from 1.38 to 1.82, indicating excellent short-term debt coverage.",
      "Net current assets (working capital) expanded by 33.8% in the final year, reaching £5.96m, which provides a substantial buffer for operational requirements.",
      "The capital structure has shifted towards a highly de-leveraged position, with total debt (short and long term) falling from £1.34m in FY23 to just £27.9k in FY25.",
      "Gearing has effectively been eliminated, dropping from 19.7% in FY23 to a negligible 0.17% in FY25, representing a very low-risk profile for lenders or buyers.",
      "While tangible fixed assets are depreciating, the growth in cash reserves (up 119% since FY23) and receivables suggests a transition to a more liquid, cash-generative business model.",
      "A potential red flag is noted in the FY25 audit qualification regarding inventory verification (£2.6m), which warrants further due diligence despite the strong balance sheet figures."
    ]
